1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:22,677
The engineering professor cried when he returned my Lamborghini. This
nigga had repaired half the greatest machines in the sky, and now he
was holding a polishing cloth to his face because my car had made him
believe again. Actual tears. One fell on the hood, and he polished it
away with his sleeve before he let himself have the next one.

2
00:00:22,927 --> 00:00:46,460
His name was Professor Atlas Bell. He was forty-six, had four arms,
and treated engines like other men treated their firstborn sons. He
stood beside the car in the morning sunlight with two hands folded,
one holding a clipboard, and the last stroking the repaired fender. It
was beautiful before, he told me. But what you did with it— He had to
stop.

3
00:00:46,710 --> 00:01:09,773
Tank leaned toward me. Nigga, you made a man cry with traffic. It
wasn't regular traffic. Nigga was crying when we got here. Maybe he
started early. No, nigga. Rosa asked that nigga what happened, and he
said your suspension. I looked at Bell. The professor nodded gravely,
like my suspension had died for his sins and risen on the third wheel.

4
00:01:10,023 --> 00:01:33,288
A magnificent structure, he said. Tank pointed at him. See? Nigga
grieving and praising at once. Let that nigga feel his feelings, I
told him. He brought my car back beautiful. Bell had restored the dark
blue paint. The police lights were now hidden beneath the front edge,
so the car looked like pure money until I decided somebody should be
nervous.

5
00:01:33,538 --> 00:01:58,403
He had reinforced the suspension for campus roads and fitted the
wheels with the academy's standard field receivers. That meant the
Lamborghini could travel along the marked sky lanes like the other
vehicles. It did not mean it could fly wherever I wanted. He explained
that last part three times. I heard him all three times. I just
refused to make my face less hopeful.

6
00:01:58,653 --> 00:02:18,549
Bell laid the clipboard on the hood and drew a blue road with a pen.
He put a little square on it. Your car. Nigga, give it some shape. He
added a triangle at the front. Tank leaned in. Now it's a refrigerator
that heard something. It is a diagram, Bell said. Of a crime against
design.

7
00:02:18,799 --> 00:02:44,073
One of the professor's hands covered the drawing while another
retrieved his polishing cloth. The third pointed at me. The fourth
pointed at Tank. Nigga had enough arms to tell both of us to shut up
and still protect his work. Inside the marked field, the receivers
support the vehicle. Outside it, they have nothing to receive. Do you
understand? Nigga, yes. Explain it back.

8
00:02:44,322 --> 00:03:09,065
Tank slapped the hood. Ooh. He assigned this nigga consequences with
oral examination. I pointed to the line. Car goes here. Correct. I
pointed beyond it. Car should not go here. Cannot. Nigga, it can go
there. You just won't like the direction. Bell took a breath.
Considered correcting me. Decided gravity could keep its small
victory. Exactly.

9
00:03:09,315 --> 00:03:33,407
Shawna had reached us in time to hear that. She took the pen and drew
a second square beside the first. What's that? I asked. The hospital
bill. Baby, that one's bigger than the car. Nigga, I included
emotional damages. Bell nodded at her drawing like somebody had
finally entered a useful number. Tank inspected both squares. Put my
ass in a circle.

10
00:03:33,657 --> 00:04:00,180
I ain't being included. You're always included, I said. That's what
I'm appealing, nigga. Bell tore off the diagram, folded it, and gave
it to Shawna. She slid it into her pocket. I watched my own operating
instructions change hands without anybody requesting the
manufacturer's consent. Now, Bell said, uncovering the car, we may
admire it. Nigga, finally a subject everybody studied.

11
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:24,814
Shawna wore a white tracksuit with my name embroidered over her heart.
Rosa wore red. Mercedes wore green leather. Porsche had found a silver
jumpsuit and a pair of boots that made a nearby man forget how stairs
worked. We going to your test, Shawna said. What test? Victor emerged
from the archway behind her. Power placement. He said it like an
execution date.

12
00:04:25,064 --> 00:04:44,637
I already got a parking place, I told him. Let's see how you perform
without a car. Nigga, ask my wife. Shawna slapped my chest and started
laughing. Victor looked up at the sky as if requesting a different
assignment from God. The placement hall was bigger inside than
outside.

13
00:04:44,887 --> 00:05:10,210
It had retractable walls, a floor divided into colored circles, and a
spectator gallery rising around all four sides. Students filled the
seats. Word of the train rescue had apparently traveled faster than
the train was supposed to. Half the crowd wore little gold paper
badges somebody had made overnight. One woman held a sign reading
ARREST ME, CAPTAIN. Shawna saw it.

14
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:32,340
The woman slowly turned it around. Storm stood in the center beside a
stone pillar holding a blue crystal. The crystal wasn't the size of a
jewel. It was the size of a man's head, cut into an uneven heart, and
its light pulsed down through the pillar into the floor. The Heart of
the Sky, she said as we approached.

15
00:05:32,590 --> 00:05:59,100
It anchors the academy's central field. Today you will be assessed
around a fractional projection of its output. I looked at the thing.
Whole school running off one diamond? A power core. It amplifies
gifts; it doesn't create them. Marcellus bent toward the crystal. He
did not touch it. His expression narrowed. Interesting cut. Voss stood
near the gallery stairs. Please keep your distance, Mr.

16
00:05:59,350 --> 00:06:27,807
Vale. Marcellus straightened. I was admiring it. Of course. Storm
clapped once. The first wall folded back, revealing a corridor full of
swinging steel blocks. Beyond it stood three platforms and a bell
suspended over a pool. Movement, she said. Judgment. Control. Rescue.
We rank useful outcomes, not destruction. Tank looked at the steel
blocks. Good. Because some nigga absolutely about to destroy
something.

17
00:06:28,058 --> 00:06:52,168
Victor went first. I gave him that much: the man was magnificent when
he stopped talking. He turned into a streak of blue light, passed
between the blocks, landed on the first platform, and sent a bolt into
a target above the second. A bridge unfolded. He crossed it, caught a
weighted rescue dummy as it fell, and reached the bell in twenty-three
seconds.

18
00:06:52,418 --> 00:07:16,489
The crowd roared. He set the dummy down carefully. Looked straight at
me. Rang the bell once more. I nodded. Clean. He seemed annoyed I
meant it. A woman named Petra Stone went next. Twenty-nine, broad
shoulders, calm eyes. She could turn her skin into white marble. She
carried the rescue dummy through a steel block instead of around it.
Her time was slower.

19
00:07:16,739 --> 00:07:43,378
The steel block's prospects were considerably worse. Mercedes stood up
clapping. Girl, yes! Petra looked up, spotted her, and nearly dropped
the dummy. Porsche leaned against the rail. You already choosing? I'm
appreciating strength. You appreciate everybody with shoulders. Only
if they use them right. Then Storm said my name. The entire gallery
stood. Nigga, I had not done anything in this room yet.

20
00:07:43,628 --> 00:08:09,719
I took off my jacket and gave it to Shawna. She smoothed my collar
with both hands. Come back with all your teeth. Baby, that's the
minimum. At the starting line, a faculty member asked whether I
required a special condition. Such as? Reduced gravity. Protective
barrier. A powered escort. Some music. He blinked. Rosa began tapping
the railing. Tank joined her. Then Porsche.

21
00:08:09,969 --> 00:08:35,231
Then half the room. A big rolling beat traveled through the hall. My
people had turned a superhero examination into the entrance to my own
heavyweight championship. Storm lifted her hand. The blocks began
swinging. I ran. First block left. Second block right. A narrow
opening appeared between them, and I went through sideways with my
shoulder almost kissing steel.

22
00:08:35,481 --> 00:08:53,383
The third descended straight at my head. I dropped under it, slid
across the floor, and came up laughing because a nigga knows when his
body has decided to make him famous. The first platform was farther
than it looked. I jumped anyway. My fingers caught the edge.

23
00:08:53,633 --> 00:09:14,836
I pulled myself up, rolled under a sweeping bar, and saw the target
Victor had struck with lightning. I had no lightning. I had shoes. I
took one off and threw it. The shoe hit the center of the target. The
bridge unfolded. Tank shouted so loud I heard him over everybody else.
Nigga used a loafer!

24
00:09:15,086 --> 00:09:28,459
I crossed in one shoe, caught the falling dummy over my shoulder, and
took the last platform in three strides. The bell hung above the pool.
Victor had flown to it. Petra had jumped from the edge.

25
00:09:28,709 --> 00:09:51,251
I threw the dummy onto the safe pad, caught its rebound with my knee,
and used the spring in the pad to launch myself up the pillar beside
the bell. My hand struck gold. The sound filled the room. Twenty-two
seconds. I landed in the pool. Nobody's masterpiece is dry all the way
through. When I surfaced, Storm was smiling.

26
00:09:51,501 --> 00:10:15,105
The faculty member stared at his clock. Victor stared at my shoe,
which was slowly sliding off the target. Shawna had both hands over
her head. That's my fucking man! I climbed out dripping. Walked to
Victor. Held out my hand. He looked at it. You used the rescue dummy
as a springboard. I rescued it first. That's not— Storm glanced at the
safe pad.

27
00:10:15,355 --> 00:10:39,634
The dummy remained entirely within the designated safety zone. Victor
shook my hand. Hard. I shook it back. Harder. We both smiled like
niggas deciding whether a friendship ought to begin with a fight. The
next test involved doors. Behind one stood a fire. Behind another, a
trapped volunteer. Behind a third, a man pretending to be an attacker.

28
00:10:39,884 --> 00:11:00,279
You had to choose in six seconds using information flashed on a
screen. I looked at the screen. Then I looked at the doors. Then I
walked up to the third door and knocked. The volunteer attacker opened
it out of surprise. I took his padded weapon. You under arrest. The
gallery exploded.

29
00:11:00,529 --> 00:11:22,198
He said, But the scenario— Nigga, you armed behind a door while people
dying in the next room. Come carry something. I put him to work.
Together we carried the trapped volunteer through the safe corridor
while Petra smothered the training fire with a wall of stone. The
faculty member tried to say assistance wasn't part of the test.

30
00:11:22,448 --> 00:11:41,167
Storm asked whether real disasters prohibited asking another adult for
help. He looked at his clipboard and discovered a deep interest in the
lower half of it. By lunch they had awarded me first place in
movement, judgment, improvisation, and something called command
presence.

31
00:11:41,416 --> 00:12:00,766
Command presence was when other niggas did what you said because it
sounded like the part of the day they should survive. I had been
practicing that since Vegas. Then the real attacker came through the
ceiling. He wore a black flight harness and a mirrored mask. Three
more followed him through the skylight.

32
00:12:01,016 --> 00:12:24,914
They fell in a line, landing around the crystal pillar with weapons
already raised. The first shot shattered a gallery lamp. Screams
replaced applause. Victor moved toward the pillar. One of the
attackers threw a dark metal hoop. It struck his chest and opened
around him, pinning his arms to his sides. His lightning flared once,
then guttered. Storm lifted her hand.

33
00:12:25,164 --> 00:12:47,368
The man in the mirrored mask held up a small device with a red light.
Wind, he said, and the south gallery falls. Beneath the south seats,
red lights blinked. Shawna was in the south gallery. So was everybody
I loved. I felt the whole room go narrow. The man saw my badge. Sit
down, officer. I looked at him.

34
00:12:47,618 --> 00:13:09,119
Nigga had chosen the wrong profession to disrespect in front of my
wife. What's your name? I asked. Your last warning. Your mama named
you terribly. His weapon moved toward me. My shoe hit his mask. The
same shoe. I had retrieved it between tests. A good object can have
more than one destiny. He stumbled.

35
00:13:09,369 --> 00:13:30,904
I crossed the space between us and hit him with every grievance I had
about being wet in public. The red device flew from his hand. Porsche
caught it over the gallery rail. She stared at the blinking light. Do
I press it? Fuck no! four of us shouted. She tucked it into her purse.
Then nobody else getting it. The room erupted.

36
00:13:31,154 --> 00:13:55,911
Petra stepped in front of the gallery stairs and turned to marble as
gunfire struck her shoulders. Mercedes dragged two frozen students
down behind the seats. Tank came over the railing like a refrigerator
deciding it had wings. He landed on one attacker, picked him up by his
harness, and introduced him to the training pool. Rosa kept people
moving. Shawna had my jacket.

37
00:13:56,161 --> 00:14:16,453
My gun was inside it. She threw the jacket. I caught it against my
chest as the masked man recovered. He lunged. I swung the whole jacket
into his face, pulled the gun free, and brought the fight to a clear
disagreement he could understand. Down. He looked at the gun. Looked
at me. Went down.

38
00:14:16,703 --> 00:14:40,953
At the pillar, another attacker struck the crystal with a forked black
instrument. Blue light cracked through the room. The floor tilted.
Students slid against the gallery rail. The crystal split down its
center. Instead of a blaze, it gave a thin, ugly flicker. Marcellus
saw it. So did Storm. Their faces told me different things about the
same bad discovery.

39
00:14:41,203 --> 00:15:05,821
The attacker cursed and tried again. Victor, trapped in the hoop,
slammed himself sideways into the man's knees. Both fell. The forked
instrument skidded toward the pool. I kicked it away before anybody
could reach it. Tank emerged from the water holding his attacker by
the collar. This nigga allergic to drowning. Thought everybody should
know. Storm's hands flashed.

40
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:30,101
With the red device safely inside Porsche's purse, the dean stopped
being patient. Wind tore the weapons out of the attackers' hands. A
pressure wave lifted all four men and pinned them against the far
wall. Their harnesses rattled. The mirrored mask broke in two.
Underneath was a lean man with a burned eyebrow and a grin too quick
for the situation.

41
00:15:30,351 --> 00:15:54,184
He looked at me. You're better than the picture. And you worse than
your introduction. Voss arrived through the side doors with six
guards. He took in the smashed skylight, the fractured crystal, the
attackers pinned to the wall. His jaw tightened before the rest of his
face followed. Finn Cinder, he said to the unmasked man. Finn's grin
faded. Chancellor. I caught that.

42
00:15:54,434 --> 00:16:18,698
Storm caught it too. You know him? she asked. A notorious sky-lane
criminal. Nigga, I said, he knew you back. Voss turned to me. My
position attracts enemies. Apparently they know which door to use. His
guards took the men from Storm's wind. Finn went quietly, but as he
passed Victor he looked at the hoop around the man's arms and almost
smiled again. Almost.

43
00:16:18,948 --> 00:16:44,428
I noticed almosts for a living. Once they were gone, Bell hurried to
the pillar with two assistants. The broken crystal had gone gray.
Storm stood over it without speaking. Marcellus touched my elbow. That
isn't the core she described. You sure? Aiden, I have spent most of my
life distinguishing beautiful things from expensive lies. Across the
hall, Victor struggled with the hoop.

44
00:16:44,678 --> 00:17:03,085
Every time he summoned electricity, its dark surface drank the light.
He was trying to make it look like he had chosen to stand there with
his elbows glued to his ribs. I went over. Hold still. I have it. You
got it around you. Different accomplishment. He stopped moving.

45
00:17:03,335 --> 00:17:27,792
Bell took one look, muttered something furious about stolen equipment,
and pressed the release concealed under its rim. The hoop opened.
Victor flexed his arms. Thank you. It came out like a little rock he
had been forced to swallow backward. Anytime. You still cheated on the
course. Nigga, you turned into lightning. I threw footwear. For the
first time, he laughed. Just briefly.

46
00:17:28,042 --> 00:17:50,118
But I saw the man hiding behind all that first-place anger, and the
man seemed like somebody I could eventually drink with. Shawna reached
me. She ran her hands over my chest, checking what bullets had failed
to do. Then she held my face and looked at me with those dark, bright
eyes. You did all that with one shoe on. I looked down.

47
00:17:50,368 --> 00:18:11,886
Still one shoe. The other lay beside the shattered mask in a little
patch of sunlight. Baby, imagine if I had dressed properly. She
started laughing, and the laugh broke the last of the fear in my ribs.
The gallery began chanting my name. Aiden. Aiden. Aiden. Somebody
added Captain. Somebody added King.

48
00:18:12,136 --> 00:18:27,758
Elias, the man from the train, stood at the front with both fists in
the air as if we had been brothers since birth. Storm raised her voice
over them. Today's assessment is concluded. Victor looked at her. The
final rankings?

49
00:18:28,008 --> 00:18:50,844
She gestured at the room: forty safe students, four captured gunmen,
one ruined crystal, my wife holding my face like I was the prize the
academy should have been competing for. Do you require them read
aloud? He considered that. Then he stepped aside and let me pick up my
shoe. On our way out, Porsche handed me the red device from her purse.

50
00:18:51,094 --> 00:19:13,018
You owe me. For saving the gallery? For not pressing a button. You
know how hard that is when it looks important? I took it. The light
had stopped blinking. On the back, beneath a scrape in the black
paint, was a tiny silver crest. A narrow tower. A downward-pointing
wing. The same crest Voss's guards wore on their shoulders.

51
00:19:13,268 --> 00:19:34,000
I closed my hand around it before anybody else saw. Come on, I said to
my people. Let's go find lunch. Tank studied my face. And after lunch?
I looked toward the doors through which the chancellor had taken my
prisoners. After lunch, nigga, I'm finding out who think this school
belong to him.

52
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:55,099
Lunch took place on a terrace where the tables floated six inches off
the ground. I asked the waiter why. He said atmosphere. I told him we
already had plenty. He laughed until he realized I meant the table
should stop drifting while I tried to cut my steak. Victor joined us
uninvited, which I considered progress.

53
00:19:55,349 --> 00:20:19,542
He sat opposite Tank and ordered enough food for three men. Petra came
with Mercedes. Porsche immediately asked whether Petra had any
brothers, sisters, cousins, or enemies with similar shoulders. Shawna
took my hand beneath the table. You really don't feel any different?
she asked. From what? The crystal. The test. All this. I turned my
hand palm up.

54
00:20:19,792 --> 00:20:44,428
There were fresh bandages over yesterday's cuts. The fingers still
belonged to a nigga who had to open his own jars. Same me. Victor
leaned forward. That makes what you did worse. Worse? More difficult
to accept. Tank laughed into his drink. At least you honest now. A
pair of uniformed campus officers approached our table. Both were
older than me.

55
00:20:44,678 --> 00:21:05,972
One had a neatly trimmed gray beard; the other could apparently see
through walls because she looked toward the kitchen and said our
second round was coming. The bearded officer saluted. Captain.
Commander Orrin Pike. Campus patrol. Sit down, Commander. I'd be
honored. He sat so fast Victor had to move his plate.

56
00:21:06,222 --> 00:21:34,405
Pike explained that the chancellor maintained a separate security
force for the lower facilities. Campus patrol could handle the sky
lanes, the shops, and the residential towers. Anything below the
island's foundation required Voss's approval. What lower facilities?
Shawna asked. Pike looked at Storm's tower before answering. A
detention and research annex. Established before the dean's
appointment. Detention for who?

57
00:21:34,655 --> 00:21:57,902
People whose powers present unusual risks. Charged with what? I asked.
He shifted in his chair. There it was. Not proof. Not even half of
proof. But enough for lunch to become something I ate while being
angry. The second officer put a folded slip beside my plate. She kept
her voice low. The four men from your hall never reached our cells.

58
00:21:58,152 --> 00:22:18,939
Victor stopped cutting his steak. I unfolded the slip. A patrol camera
had captured Finn Cinder boarding a black car under his own power. No
cuffs. Voss's guard held the door for him. Pike looked ashamed enough
to make me trust him a little. I thought you should know. I put the
picture in my pocket.

59
00:22:19,189 --> 00:22:24,181
Commander, nigga, you just earned yourself a very interesting
afternoon.
